Overview
This assignment demonstrates the use of machine learning classification techniques on two different datasets: Asphalt Crack Classification and Email Spam Classification.

Part A – Asphalt Crack Classification
The objective is to classify asphalt images into Crack and Non-Crack categories.

Steps
* Image resizing and grayscale conversion
* Extraction of intensity-based features
* Canny edge detection for feature extraction
* Creation of improved features using multiple Canny thresholds
* Training and comparison of classification models

Models
* Logistic Regression
* Random Forest
* Support Vector Machine (SVM)

Evaluation
Models are evaluated using:
* Accuracy
* Precision
* Recall
* F1 Score
* Confusion Matrix
* Training and prediction time

Baseline and improved features are compared to study their effect on model performance.


Part B – Email Spam Classification
The objective is to classify emails as Spam or Not Spam using the `emails.csv` dataset.

Steps
* Dataset inspection
* Missing-value and duplicate checking
* Feature and target separation
* Stratified train-test split
* Model training and evaluation

Models
* Logistic Regression
* Random Forest
* Linear SVM

Evaluation
The models are compared using accuracy, precision, recall, F1 score, confusion matrices, classification reports, and execution time.

Conclusion
The assignment demonstrates the complete machine learning workflow, from preprocessing and feature extraction to model training, evaluation, comparison, and result generation for both image and email classification tasks.
